#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110295 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110674 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f67c3319-1153-51ed-a57a-f85c06c7e76c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Points on Intersecting Lines Are Collinear"}] :question/id #uuid "a042ba66-3567-5b06-84e6-344ad0043bbc" :question/math-academy-id "e-10748" :question/problem "![](images/2f/2f6d703c604c780da8c97a012b94e75f06a55aa8b6e706a1097dc33ff193e88c.png)\n\nGiven the picture shown above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The points $K$, $N$, and $Z$ are collinear\n2. The points $K$, $P$, and $J$ are collinear" :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is false. We can't draw a straight line that passes through these three points.\n\n![](images/39/390f01ec8631f4c4eca0f391dd5b1c2f9e450e94d3bd992e6046c42dff0fc1e8.png)\n\n- Statement II is true. There is a straight line that passes through these three points.\n\n![](images/d9/d9d250f402d238388931ec077d17afe65b248d245ae6333f9cb150c18288ccce.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110296 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110675 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9ef4e321-841e-5933-b5e4-ff7dab6c5275" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Collinear Points on a Grid"}] :question/id #uuid "76902823-634d-5525-afc5-5f2a98cea481" :question/math-academy-id "e-10749" :question/problem "Which of the diagrams below shows three collinear points?\n\n![](images/c0/c0df27c96da9f9c285438faee93652f81362fe91a51dc28e02ec0e2e9ff42177.png)" :question/worked-solution "Three (or more) points are collinear if a straight line passes through all points.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our diagrams in turn.\n\n- Diagram I shows three points that are *not* collinear. We can't draw a straight line that passes through all three points.\n\n![](images/49/4967d8325f8ed8415a8404286d29ff97eb65cd6926ed1ca27a943178aee1a3cc.png)\n\n- Diagram II shows three collinear points. There is a straight line that passes through all three of these points.\n\n![](images/af/af746af6fba54f69570f5dcfa38fbbb4cffd290080cc45deec433bc5266aa75e.png)\n\n- Diagram III shows three points that are *not* collinear. We can't draw a straight line that passes through all three points.\n\n![](images/c0/c0d9d178c5be09aa7f6ad1927c6f8e930154cf077aabbd18a765820babd63069.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110905 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110674 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f67c3319-1153-51ed-a57a-f85c06c7e76c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Points on Intersecting Lines Are Collinear"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab463a2d-5905-58f7-af68-2bb4b2f11fa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107322} {:answer/id #uuid "ca5b688b-0323-5661-8259-9b195cde3e07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107323} {:answer/id #uuid "e27df00f-7404-5963-a875-5f57e801702e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107324} {:answer/id #uuid "eb426f3b-b1df-57a8-8520-bb401013cc4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107325} {:answer/id #uuid "40830f1d-0ff2-52bd-bc13-247a6b6c50f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107326}] :answer-field/id #uuid "d078c165-bd3b-5097-be93-c04451228952" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107321}] :question/id #uuid "d5df118a-6629-591e-bac9-243a7536e271" :question/math-academy-id "q-13445" :question/problem "![](images/36/36ea34524b2ca277e8061441492711d36c8065e765d519d85d4008da97c3f8b3.png)\n\nConsider the figure shown above. Which of the following triplets of points are collinear?\n\n1. $M, N, R$\n2. $P, S, T$\n3. $O, P, S$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110929 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110675 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9ef4e321-841e-5933-b5e4-ff7dab6c5275" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Collinear Points on a Grid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ec68db2-863b-55ad-8b69-eefdfc5401ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107466} {:answer/id #uuid "af56ea0b-013c-519d-a19e-24c5eecb6eb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107467} {:answer/id #uuid "269504ce-2a6a-5ccd-9cf4-5b401742671b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107468} {:answer/id #uuid "5b210728-6a80-5b8f-97a2-05caf904c89a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107469} {:answer/id #uuid "7ddee60b-d64d-5874-a34e-03b6baff8ee0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107470}] :answer-field/id #uuid "e907c4ba-8343-5fdd-abfe-8b39f70e8112" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107465}] :question/id #uuid "4ea9e0d7-7c8f-5224-8f6f-e5c31c36ab4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-155503" :question/problem "![](images/bb/bb96a7692787ca6e055b41d4f1599b87baa1ea331544ea42235a7131343c76e3.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams above shows three collinear points?"}]}
